  <prompt>
    Replace the SPE owning-app certificate with the federated credential created on 2026-10-02: prove it works from
    inside Azure first, then make L2 acquire owning-app tokens from the Worker's managed identity, make H0 and the H13 T6
    trap probe check things that can actually pass, register `Spaarke Model 1` in Spaarke's tenant, and point the Worker
    at the container type.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer on the L2 provisioning control plane, expert in Entra workload identity federation,
    Azure.Identity and Microsoft Graph SharePoint Embedded APIs. Follow ADR-028 A4 strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A Model 1 run's H0 passes the SPE owner check without any certificate or stored secret; H8 creates and verifies the
    customer container as the `Spaarke SPE Model 1 Owner` app using a token obtained through the Worker UAMI's federated
    credential; H13's T6 probe makes an app-only call that succeeds for a correctly configured stamp; `Spaarke Model 1`
    is registered in Spaarke's tenant; the Worker (dev) is configured with `{containerTypeId, ownerAppId}`; no document
    or skill tells an operator to create an owning-app certificate.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      G28: H0 rejects every run because L2 expected a password-less base64 PFX `SPE-OwnerCert-Pfx` in the platform vault
      (`SpeContainerOptions.ContainerTypeOwners` → `SpeConfidentialClientGraphFactory` builds a `ClientCertificateCredential`;
      `KeyVaultCertBootstrapProbe` checks the secret exists and is ≥ 24 h old) and none exists. Owner D16 (2026-10-02):
      use MI-FIC — ADR-028 A4's default credential; no ADR-028 amendment (spec row → path C). Done live 2026-10-02 with the
      operator identity: app `Spaarke SPE Model 1 Owner` (appId `bfac7f6e-9fa0-4664-8492-c7a1dfe73d5e`, single-tenant),
      Graph `FileStorageContainer.Selected` + `FileStorageContainerTypeReg.Selected` (Application) consented, FIC
      `sprk-controlplane-dev-uami-assertion` (subject = principalId `38f7693f-e6e2-4a3e-9acf-7f9e29dd4044` of
      `sprk-controlplane-dev-uami`, client id `965a4a01-01e1-442b-97a6-6a98308018b3`; structure verified, token exchange
      NOT yet tested — only possible from compute carrying the UAMI). Researcher findings
      (`.claude/agent-memory/researcher/spe-owning-app-mi-as-fic-2026-10-02.md`): FIC tokens are client assertions
      (`appidacr`/`azpacr` = 2), same shape as a certificate; container-type registration is now documented only as Graph
      v1.0 `PUT /storage/fileStorage/containerTypeRegistrations/{id}`; the legacy SharePoint REST registration returns
      `apiNotFound` in this tenant. Separately, the H13 T6 probe calls app-only `GET /storage/fileStorage/containerTypes`,
      which is documented to return 403 app-only — it could never pass.
    </background>
