    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Worker MI-FIC client assertion" location="Handlers/Credentials/WorkerDataverseCredentialFactory.cs">
        The Worker already exchanges its UAMI token (audience api://AzureADTokenExchange) for an app token via a client
        assertion. Copy that mechanism; do not introduce a second way to obtain the UAMI assertion.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A4 + owner D16">
      Every owning-app token L2 acquires in this task comes from a client assertion fed by the Worker UAMI. No certificate,
      no client secret, no Key Vault read for the owning-app credential. Do not keep the certificate path as a silent
      fallback; if the live probe fails, escalation 1 applies.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="live-change discipline (root CLAUDE.md — outward-facing actions)">
      Before each live action — creating any temporary Azure resource for the probe, the registration `PUT`, the
      `platform-controlplane` deployment, the Worker code deployment — state exactly what will change and get the owner's
      confirmation. Read-only calls need no confirmation. Delete any temporary resource the probe created.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/provisioning.md § KV credential lifecycle (BINDING)">
      No Key Vault secret is created, deleted or purged. The soft-deleted `spe-app-cert` and every E-1 secret
      (`spe-owning-app-secret` etc.) are untouched. Do not add any federated credential other than the one already on the
      owning app.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">
      Per-customer BFF grants on the registration (G9) are T227 — the registration created here grants only the owning
      app itself. `spaarke-constants.yaml` gets the Model 1 container type id under the env key the
      `/provision-environment` skill reads for Model 1 stamps; the file's stale trial-era structure is T227 (G2). No change
      to `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api` (its SpeAdmin secret path is E-1, unchanged).
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The live probe cannot obtain an owning-app token through the FIC, or Graph/SPE rejects the FIC-acquired token on any call this task needs → STOP. Report the error and the decoded token claims (no token values). The certificate is then ADR-028 A4's sanctioned alternative for a stated reason — that is an owner decision, not an implementation choice.</trigger>
    <trigger>The container type the owner created is not `standard`, is owned by an app other than `bfac7f6e-…`, or has no billing attached → STOP before registering it.</trigger>
    <trigger>Graph's registration contract (body shape, permission names) differs from the researcher note in a way that changes what is granted → STOP and report before sending the PUT.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0">Precondition: owner has sent the `Spaarke Model 1` container type id. Read-only: `GET` the container type (delegated, via a tool that has the scope, or the SharePoint admin center) and confirm name, owning app `bfac7f6e-…`, `standard`, billing attached. 0 behind origin/master.</step>
    <step order="1">LIVE PROBE (confirm first). From compute that carries `sprk-controlplane-dev-uami` — preferred `az webapp ssh` into the Worker's app container (not the SCM container); otherwise a throwaway ACI with the UAMI attached — obtain the UAMI assertion, exchange it for an owning-app Graph token (tenant `a221a95e-…`, client `bfac7f6e-…`), record `appidacr`/`azpacr`/`roles` claims (never the token), then: `GET /storage/fileStorage/containerTypeRegistrations/{id}`; if not registered, `PUT` the registration granting the owning app itself (confirm the body first); `GET /storage/fileStorage/containers?$filter=containerTypeId eq {id}`. Record results in the POML notes. Escalation 1 if anything fails.</step>
    <step order="2">Code — credential: `SpeConfidentialClientGraphFactory` builds a client-assertion credential fed by the Worker UAMI (reference: `WorkerDataverseCredentialFactory`); `SpeContainerOptions` owner entries become `{ContainerTypeId, OwnerAppId}` (vault/secret properties and their validation removed; GUID + duplicate checks kept).</step>
    <step order="3">Code — H0: replace `KeyVaultCertBootstrapProbe` with an owner-credential probe: owner entry exists for the run's `containerTypeId`; an owning-app token can be acquired; the registration `GET` succeeds. Retire the 24 h age gate and `spe-cert-bootstrap-missing`; distinct Resumable codes for (a) no owner entry, (b) token exchange failed, (c) container type not registered. Update H0's rejection-code documentation and every consumer of the old code (grep: skill, docs).</step>
    <step order="4">Code — H13 T6: replace the app-only `GET /storage/fileStorage/containerTypes` probe with app-only `GET /storage/fileStorage/containers?$filter=containerTypeId eq {id}`, passing when the call succeeds and the run's container is listed.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests for steps 2–4 (see test-scope criterion). Build + run ControlPlane.Tests and ArchTests.</step>
    <step order="6">Configuration: Worker Bicep emits only `ContainerTypeId` + `OwnerAppId` per owner entry; `platform-controlplane-dev.bicepparam` `speContainerTypeOwners = [{ containerTypeId: '{id}', ownerAppId: 'bfac7f6e-9fa0-4664-8492-c7a1dfe73d5e' }]`; recompile JSON (`--outfile`); `spaarke-constants.yaml` Model 1 container type id.</step>
    <step order="7">DEPLOY (confirm first): `platform-controlplane` to dev, then the Worker code. Verify read-only: Worker app settings carry the owner entry and no `OwnerCert*` setting; Worker healthy; trigger nothing else.</step>
    <step order="8">Docs: topology runbook rewritten for MI-FIC (owning app → consent via `appRoleAssignedTo` → FIC → container type in admin center → registration via Graph v1.0) incl. its drift (H8 "uses the BFF UAMI", FIC "added in Step 8", grants `POST` vs per-item `PUT`); topology doc owning-app credential section; inventory; deployment guide; `.claude` constraints/patterns/skill (main session) + CHANGELOG; spec ADR-028 E-1 row notes the probe result; plan §4 G28 closed.</step>
    <step order="9">Step 9.5 gates (code-review + adr-check — auth-sensitive). Close: POML notes, TASK-INDEX `✅ [done]`, current-task.md, drift check. Commit + push.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="az">Graph via `az rest` (read-only checks), `az webapp ssh`, `az bicep build --outfile`, deployments (after confirmation)</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build + test ControlPlane and ArchTests</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">Scripts, check-task-status-drift.ps1</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">SpeConfidentialClientGraphFactory, SpeContainerOptions, H0 owner-credential probe (replaces KeyVaultCertBootstrapProbe), T6 probe, rejection codes, DI</output>
